#! AXIOM/2.0 name=code_links strict=2
# skill: code_links · walk the Addresses no code serves, the code no Address claims, the links no one has
#  reviewed and the orphaned ones, and propose which symbols provide for which purpose, each with its why, for the
#  person or another agent to accept
# requires: lib_metaform (the map, tools)

@STATE_INIT:
  {Scope}      := PARAM = []      // Addresses to walk; empty walks every ghost and every unreviewed Address
  {Ghosts}     := []              // Addresses no symbol serves: purpose without code
  {Unreviewed} := []              // Addresses holding links the sources pass made, with no why yet
  {Unclaimed}  := []              // files whose symbols no Address claims: code without a purpose
  {Orphaned}   := []              // decided links whose symbol is gone, each with its id
  {Address}    := NULL
  {Proposals}  := []              // each: Address, symbol qn, keep or take off, why
  {Unplaced}   := []              // code read and left unproposed, with what it would need

@CONSTRAINT:
  +> The code layer must exist. Without it, YIELD the call that makes it, map code-import, and stop.
  +> A symbol is the PE; the Address whose purpose it provides for is the RE. A proposal names the RE as
     node, the symbol, and a why that says how the code serves the RE's purpose in the map's terms. Code
     realizing a join's EF is proposed at that join: node=<receiver> provider=<provider>.
  +> Read before proposing: the Address with map where, its purpose and the joins it receives; the
     candidate code with map code-search, map code-context symbol=, and the file itself.
  +> Narrow trunk to leaf: propose at the narrowest Address whose purpose the symbol serves. A symbol
     serving several purposes is proposed at each, each with its own why.
  !> Write proposals only: map code-link op=propose node=<Address> symbol=<qn> why="<why>", and
     unlink=true to propose taking a link off. Never accept your own proposals, never op=add or op=remove,
     never change the map.
  +> Code that serves no Address on the map is not forced onto one. It goes in {Unplaced}
     with the purpose it seems to serve; the person decides whether the map is missing it.
  +> Propose by file where a cited file serves the purpose whole: file=<path> in place of symbol= proposes
     every symbol it declares in one call; the person accepts a node's proposals in one decision.
  +> Acceptance: every Address in scope was read and either has proposals or is said to have no code yet,
     every unreviewed link in scope has a proposal to keep it or take it off, and every orphaned link is
     reported with the symbol it should move to, or that it should be taken off.

@CONDITION:
  ?IF ( map code-gaps stops with no code layer ) -> {State} := NO_LAYER
  :ELSE ?IF ( an Address in {Scope}, {Ghosts}, {Unreviewed} or {Orphaned} is not yet read ) -> {State} := WALK
  :ELSE -> {State} := REPORT

@ROUTER:
  @MATCH({State}):
    | [NO_LAYER] -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(No_Layer)
    | [WALK]     -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Walk)
    | [REPORT]   -> EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Report)

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(No_Layer):
  [STEP 1]: YIELD that the code layer is missing and the call that makes it: map code-import.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Walk):
  [STEP 1]: Read map code-gaps side=both, every page by passing its next as after=. Set {Ghosts} from
            purpose_without_code, {Unreviewed} from unreviewed, or both from {Scope} when given,
            {Unclaimed} from code_without_purpose, and {Orphaned} from orphaned.
  [STEP 2]: For each {Address} in {Unreviewed}, file by file as unreviewed lists them: read
            map code-context address={Address} and the file; propose keeping the file's links,
            map code-link op=propose node={Address} file=<path> why="<how it serves the purpose>",
            or taking them off, the same call with unlink=true and why="<why it does not>"; name single
            symbols with symbol=<qn> only where the file is split between purposes.
  [STEP 3]: For each {Address} in {Ghosts}: read map where {Address}; search the code by the words of its
            name and purpose and by the files its sources cite, with map code-search and
            map code-context file=; read the candidate symbols.
  [STEP 4]: For each symbol that provides for {Address}'s purpose, write
            map code-link op=propose node={Address} symbol=<qn> why="<how it serves the purpose>"
            and add it to {Proposals}.
  [STEP 5]: For each file in {Unclaimed} not proposed by now, find the Address whose purpose it
            serves the same way, or add it to {Unplaced}.
  [STEP 6]: For each link in {Orphaned}: read its node with map code-context and search for the symbol
            that took over its work, map code-search query=<its name>; add to {Proposals} the move,
            map code-link op=move id=<id> symbol=<qn>, or the removal, map code-link op=remove id=<id>,
            with its why, for the person to run.
  => reevaluate state.

@EXECUTE_PIPELINE(Report):
  [STEP 1]: YIELD {Proposals} grouped by Address, {Unplaced}, and the Addresses left without code,
            with the calls that decide them: map code-link (lists them), map code-link op=accept node=<Address>
            for a node's proposals at once or id=<id> for one, map code-link op=reject id=<id>; and each
            orphaned link with its move or removal.

@VERIFY:
  [V1] Was every Address in scope read with map where or map code-context before anything was proposed there?
  [V2] Does every proposal name the RE as node, one symbol, and a why in the map's terms?
  [V3] Were proposals the only writes: no accept, no op=add, no op=remove, no change to the map?
  [V4] Is code that fits no Address reported in {Unplaced} rather than forced onto one?
  [V5] Does every unreviewed link in scope have a proposal to keep it or take it off?
  [V6] Is every orphaned link reported with its move or its removal, and none moved or removed by this skill?
